@prefix mhpkg_schema: <https://openenergyplatform.org/schema/mhpkg/> .
@prefix mhpo: <https://purl.org/mhpo/ontology/> .
@prefix obo: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/> .
@prefix oeo: <https://openenergyplatform.org/ontology/oeo/> .
@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix sh: <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

mhpo:MHPO_00020003 a sh:NodeShape ;
    rdfs:comment """A municipal heat plan — Kommunale Wärmeplanung, WPG §23. MHPO puts it under CCO `plan specification` and asserts that it has as parts an aggregated inventory analysis, an aggregated potential analysis, a target scenario, an implementation measure and an implementation strategy.
This slice models the target scenario and the aggregated inventory analysis. The other three parts are not modelled yet, which is not the same as not being in the model. The potential analysis appears in the 2026-09-15 Termboard draft but holds nothing there; it is `deferred` in `../model/termboard_mapping.yaml`.
⚠️ `has_part` now takes either part, so the generated shape can no longer say "exactly one target scenario" — LinkML emits `sh:or` over the classes and no qualified cardinality. That rule, and "at most one inventory analysis", are in the hand-written `mhpkg_context.shacl.ttl`.""" ;
    sh:closed true ;
    sh:ignoredProperties ( rdf:type ) ;
    sh:property [ sh:datatype xsd:string ;
            sh:description "The human-readable name, in German. Umlauts live here and never in an IRI — the IRI policy keeps identity ASCII-only and puts the German in the label, where it is unambiguous and universally supported." ;
            sh:maxCount 1 ;
            sh:minCount 1 ;
            sh:nodeKind sh:Literal ;
            sh:order 1 ;
            sh:path rdfs:label ],
        [ sh:description "BFO `has part`. MHPO declares this object property and already asserts `municipal heat plan SubClassOf has part some target scenario`, so this slot restates an axiom the ontology holds rather than inventing a relation." ;
            sh:minCount 1 ;
            sh:or ( [ sh:class mhpo:MHPO_00020007 ] [ sh:class mhpo:MHPO_00020005 ] ) ;
            sh:order 3 ;
            sh:path obo:BFO_0000051 ],
        [ sh:datatype xsd:date ;
            sh:description """The plan's publication date. This is not free metadata — the IRI policy makes it the Tier-2 discriminator, so it is part of the plan's identity and a shape that lets it drift lets the IRI drift with it.
NEAR MISS — OEO declares domain `report` (obo:IAO_0000088) and range `xsd:dateTime`. MHPO puts `municipal heat plan` under CCO `plan specification`, not under `report`, and a date is not a dateTime. Closer than the three above, but still borrowed.""" ;
            sh:maxCount 1 ;
            sh:minCount 1 ;
            sh:nodeKind sh:Literal ;
            sh:order 2 ;
            sh:path oeo:OEO_00390096 ],
        [ sh:description "The instance IRI, minted by the three-tier pure function of the IRI policy." ;
            sh:maxCount 1 ;
            sh:nodeKind sh:IRI ;
            sh:order 0 ;
            sh:path mhpkg_schema:id ],
        [ sh:class oeo:OEO_00030022 ;
            sh:description """OEO `has organisation` — "a relation that holds between an information content entity and the organisation in which it was created". Domain fits: MHPO's `municipal heat plan` is an information content entity by way of CCO.
Its declared range is not `organisation` but `has role some organisation role`, i.e. OEO reifies the organisation's involvement into a role. This slot deliberately points at the organisation directly and does not model the role, because which role a body plays — commissioning authority versus contracted planner — has no term yet. See TERM REQUEST 3.""" ;
            sh:minCount 1 ;
            sh:nodeKind sh:IRI ;
            sh:order 4 ;
            sh:path oeo:OEO_00000510 ] ;
    sh:targetClass mhpo:MHPO_00020003 .

mhpo:MHPO_00020017 a sh:NodeShape ;
    rdfs:comment """A municipality area — Gemeindegebiet. MHPO puts it under OEO `region` and gives it a `municipality area role`.
Present in the slice but UNREACHABLE from the plan: no cited term relates a plan to the area it plans. See TERM REQUEST 1. Its AGS is carried by its IRI.""" ;
    sh:closed true ;
    sh:ignoredProperties ( rdf:type ) ;
    sh:property [ sh:datatype xsd:string ;
            sh:description "The human-readable name, in German. Umlauts live here and never in an IRI — the IRI policy keeps identity ASCII-only and puts the German in the label, where it is unambiguous and universally supported." ;
            sh:maxCount 1 ;
            sh:minCount 1 ;
            sh:nodeKind sh:Literal ;
            sh:order 1 ;
            sh:path rdfs:label ],
        [ sh:description "The instance IRI, minted by the three-tier pure function of the IRI policy." ;
            sh:maxCount 1 ;
            sh:nodeKind sh:IRI ;
            sh:order 0 ;
            sh:path mhpkg_schema:id ] ;
    sh:targetClass mhpo:MHPO_00020017 .

oeo:OEO_00030022 a sh:NodeShape ;
    rdfs:comment """An organisation. Used for both the planning authority and the contracted planner, because no term distinguishes the two roles — see TERM REQUEST 3.
A municipality acting as planning authority is NOT a second entity: `Stadt Kassel, der Bürgermeister` is the municipality in a role, and the IRI policy gives it the Tier-1 municipality IRI. Only bodies with no register key are minted here.""" ;
    sh:closed true ;
    sh:ignoredProperties ( rdf:type ) ;
    sh:property [ sh:datatype xsd:string ;
            sh:description "The human-readable name, in German. Umlauts live here and never in an IRI — the IRI policy keeps identity ASCII-only and puts the German in the label, where it is unambiguous and universally supported." ;
            sh:maxCount 1 ;
            sh:minCount 1 ;
            sh:nodeKind sh:Literal ;
            sh:order 1 ;
            sh:path rdfs:label ],
        [ sh:description "The instance IRI, minted by the three-tier pure function of the IRI policy." ;
            sh:maxCount 1 ;
            sh:nodeKind sh:IRI ;
            sh:order 0 ;
            sh:path mhpkg_schema:id ] ;
    sh:targetClass oeo:OEO_00030022 .

oeo:OEO_00140127 a sh:NodeShape ;
    rdfs:comment """A share — Anteil. OEO's `fraction value`: a relational quantity value with a fraction as its unit. Termboard's `share`, drawn in the target scenario as the share of one energy carrier in the final energy consumption of all of them.
🔴 INCOMPLETE BY CONSTRUCTION: what a share is a share OF is TERM REQUEST 7. Until OEO relates a quantity value to its numerator and denominator, a FractionValue carries its numerator's carrier, sector and year directly, which says WHICH share it is but not of what.""" ;
    sh:closed true ;
    sh:ignoredProperties ( rdf:type ) ;
    sh:property [ sh:description "OEO `covers sector`. Same mismatch as `covers_energy_carrier` — declared domain `study`. WPG Annex 2 III.1 requires the final energy consumption differentiated by final energy sector, so the slot is unavoidable; only the relation is borrowed." ;
            sh:in ( oeo:OEO_00000214 oeo:OEO_00000227 oeo:OEO_00000128 ) ;
            sh:maxCount 1 ;
            sh:order 4 ;
            sh:path oeo:OEO_00000505 ],
        [ sh:description "The instance IRI, minted by the three-tier pure function of the IRI policy." ;
            sh:maxCount 1 ;
            sh:nodeKind sh:IRI ;
            sh:order 0 ;
            sh:path mhpkg_schema:id ],
        [ sh:description """OEO `covers energy carrier`.
MISMATCH — its declared domain is `study` (oeo:OEO_00020011), and the subject here is a consumption value, not a study. OWL domains are inferential rather than constraining, so a reasoner will not complain; it will silently infer that every MHPKG consumption value IS a study. SHACL cannot see this at all. Recorded as a term request rather than worked around.""" ;
            sh:in ( oeo:OEO_00000292 oeo:OEO_00000211 oeo:OEO_00000220 oeo:OEO_00010214 oeo:OEO_00020050 ) ;
            sh:maxCount 1 ;
            sh:order 3 ;
            sh:path oeo:OEO_00000523 ],
        [ sh:datatype xsd:integer ;
            sh:description """The year the value is stated for. WPG Annex 2 III requires the target-scenario indicators for 2030, 2035, 2040 and 2045 unless otherwise specified; an inventory analysis states them for a past base year.
The floor was 2024 while only target scenarios held values. The 2026-09-15 draft puts the same value classes into the aggregated inventory analysis too, whose base years lie in the past, and a generated shape constrains a CLASS, not the container it sits in — so the floor here is now 1990 (the Kyoto base year, the earliest a German inventory reports against), and "a target-scenario value is for 2024 or later" moved to the hand-written `mhpkg_context.shacl.ttl`, which can follow the edge from the scenario to its values.
MISMATCH, and the worst of the three — OEO `has scenario year value` declares domain `scenario factsheet` (oeo:OEO_00000365) AND range `xsd:dateTime`. This slot uses it on a consumption value with an `xsd:integer`, so both ends are wrong. A year is a temporal region, and BFO has `one-dimensional temporal region`; what is missing is a relation from a value to it.""" ;
            sh:maxCount 1 ;
            sh:maxInclusive 2100 ;
            sh:minCount 1 ;
            sh:minInclusive 1990 ;
            sh:nodeKind sh:Literal ;
            sh:order 6 ;
            sh:path oeo:OEO_00020440 ],
        [ sh:datatype xsd:float ;
            sh:description "A percentage. Out of range either way is an extraction error, not data." ;
            sh:maxCount 1 ;
            sh:maxInclusive 100 ;
            sh:minCount 1 ;
            sh:minInclusive 0 ;
            sh:nodeKind sh:Literal ;
            sh:order 1 ;
            sh:path oeo:OEO_00140178 ],
        [ sh:description """OEO `covers technology` — Termboard's `refers to technology`. Optional: WPG Annex 2 III asks for carriers and sectors, not technologies, but heat plans break consumption and emissions down by heat generation technology often enough that the 2026-09-15 draft draws it on every value.
MISMATCH — declared domain `study`, exactly like `covers energy carrier` and `covers sector`. Folded into TERM REQUEST 4.""" ;
            sh:in ( oeo:OEO_00020308 oeo:OEO_00020486 oeo:OEO_00020307 oeo:OEO_00020306 oeo:OEO_00020487 oeo:OEO_00020491 oeo:OEO_00020490 oeo:OEO_00020493 oeo:OEO_00020492 ) ;
            sh:maxCount 1 ;
            sh:order 5 ;
            sh:path oeo:OEO_00390101 ],
        [ sh:description "OEO `has unit`, domain `quantity value`, range `unit`. Exact fit." ;
            sh:in ( obo:UO_0000187 ) ;
            sh:maxCount 1 ;
            sh:minCount 1 ;
            sh:order 2 ;
            sh:path oeo:OEO_00040010 ] ;
    sh:targetClass oeo:OEO_00140127 .

mhpo:MHPO_00020005 a sh:NodeShape ;
    rdfs:comment """The aggregated inventory analysis — aggregierte Bestandsanalyse, WPG Annex 2 I. The current state the target scenario departs from: consumption and emissions for a past base year. MHPO asserts a municipal heat plan has one as a part.
Holds the same value classes as the target scenario, which is why the base-year floor on `has_scenario_year_value` had to drop — see that slot.""" ;
    sh:closed true ;
    sh:ignoredProperties ( rdf:type ) ;
    sh:property [ sh:description "The instance IRI, minted by the three-tier pure function of the IRI policy." ;
            sh:maxCount 1 ;
            sh:nodeKind sh:IRI ;
            sh:order 0 ;
            sh:path mhpkg_schema:id ],
        [ sh:datatype xsd:string ;
            sh:description "The human-readable name, in German. Umlauts live here and never in an IRI — the IRI policy keeps identity ASCII-only and puts the German in the label, where it is unambiguous and universally supported." ;
            sh:maxCount 1 ;
            sh:minCount 1 ;
            sh:nodeKind sh:Literal ;
            sh:order 1 ;
            sh:path rdfs:label ],
        [ sh:description """OEO `has quantity value` — "a relation between an entity and a quantity value". Declares no domain, so using it on a target scenario adds no unintended inference.
Note that MHPO asserts nothing here. Its `target scenario` definition says the scenario "uses indicators to describe" the goal, and its comment enumerates the seven WPG Annex 2 III indicators, but no axiom connects a scenario to a value. This slot is the first place the data shape goes beyond what the T-Box states.""" ;
            sh:minCount 1 ;
            sh:or ( [ sh:class oeo:OEO_00050016 ] [ sh:class oeo:OEO_00340065 ] ) ;
            sh:order 2 ;
            sh:path oeo:OEO_00140002 ] ;
    sh:targetClass mhpo:MHPO_00020005 .

mhpo:MHPO_00020007 a sh:NodeShape ;
    rdfs:comment """The target scenario — Zielszenario, WPG Annex 2 III. An objective specification that uses indicators to describe how a heat supply from renewable energy or unavoidable waste heat is to be achieved.
Termboard draws its values as `has part`; the schema keeps OEO `has quantity value`, as decided in MH-06 — `../model/termboard_mapping.yaml` records the translation.""" ;
    sh:closed true ;
    sh:ignoredProperties ( rdf:type ) ;
    sh:property [ sh:description """OEO `has quantity value` — "a relation between an entity and a quantity value". Declares no domain, so using it on a target scenario adds no unintended inference.
Note that MHPO asserts nothing here. Its `target scenario` definition says the scenario "uses indicators to describe" the goal, and its comment enumerates the seven WPG Annex 2 III indicators, but no axiom connects a scenario to a value. This slot is the first place the data shape goes beyond what the T-Box states.""" ;
            sh:minCount 1 ;
            sh:or ( [ sh:class oeo:OEO_00050016 ] [ sh:class oeo:OEO_00340065 ] [ sh:class oeo:OEO_00140127 ] ) ;
            sh:order 2 ;
            sh:path oeo:OEO_00140002 ],
        [ sh:datatype xsd:string ;
            sh:description "The human-readable name, in German. Umlauts live here and never in an IRI — the IRI policy keeps identity ASCII-only and puts the German in the label, where it is unambiguous and universally supported." ;
            sh:maxCount 1 ;
            sh:minCount 1 ;
            sh:nodeKind sh:Literal ;
            sh:order 1 ;
            sh:path rdfs:label ],
        [ sh:description "The instance IRI, minted by the three-tier pure function of the IRI policy." ;
            sh:maxCount 1 ;
            sh:nodeKind sh:IRI ;
            sh:order 0 ;
            sh:path mhpkg_schema:id ] ;
    sh:targetClass mhpo:MHPO_00020007 .

oeo:OEO_00050016 a sh:NodeShape ;
    rdfs:comment """A final energy consumption value — Endenergieverbrauch. OEO defines it as an energy consumption value about energy delivered to and consumed by end users, and it is exactly indicator 1 of WPG Annex 2 III.
Its identity is its coordinates and not its magnitude: the same plan, indicator, carrier, year and aggregation always mint the same IRI, so a corrected figure updates this node.""" ;
    sh:closed true ;
    sh:ignoredProperties ( rdf:type ) ;
    sh:property [ sh:description """OEO `covers technology` — Termboard's `refers to technology`. Optional: WPG Annex 2 III asks for carriers and sectors, not technologies, but heat plans break consumption and emissions down by heat generation technology often enough that the 2026-09-15 draft draws it on every value.
MISMATCH — declared domain `study`, exactly like `covers energy carrier` and `covers sector`. Folded into TERM REQUEST 4.""" ;
            sh:in ( oeo:OEO_00020308 oeo:OEO_00020486 oeo:OEO_00020307 oeo:OEO_00020306 oeo:OEO_00020487 oeo:OEO_00020491 oeo:OEO_00020490 oeo:OEO_00020493 oeo:OEO_00020492 ) ;
            sh:maxCount 1 ;
            sh:order 5 ;
            sh:path oeo:OEO_00390101 ],
        [ sh:datatype xsd:float ;
            sh:description "A consumption cannot be negative. This is the one constraint in the whole slice that comes from the domain rather than from a term — and it is exactly the kind of thing the rejected \"generate SHACL from MHPO\" route could never have produced, because OWL is open-world and carries no such assertion." ;
            sh:maxCount 1 ;
            sh:minCount 1 ;
            sh:minInclusive 0 ;
            sh:nodeKind sh:Literal ;
            sh:order 1 ;
            sh:path oeo:OEO_00140178 ],
        [ sh:description "OEO `covers sector`. Same mismatch as `covers_energy_carrier` — declared domain `study`. WPG Annex 2 III.1 requires the final energy consumption differentiated by final energy sector, so the slot is unavoidable; only the relation is borrowed." ;
            sh:in ( oeo:OEO_00000214 oeo:OEO_00000227 oeo:OEO_00000128 ) ;
            sh:maxCount 1 ;
            sh:minCount 1 ;
            sh:order 4 ;
            sh:path oeo:OEO_00000505 ],
        [ sh:description "OEO `has aggregation type`. Declares no domain, so no unintended inference." ;
            sh:in ( oeo:OEO_00140070 oeo:OEO_00140071 oeo:OEO_00140069 oeo:OEO_00140072 oeo:OEO_00140073 ) ;
            sh:maxCount 1 ;
            sh:minCount 1 ;
            sh:order 7 ;
            sh:path oeo:OEO_00390023 ],
        [ sh:description """OEO `covers energy carrier`.
MISMATCH — its declared domain is `study` (oeo:OEO_00020011), and the subject here is a consumption value, not a study. OWL domains are inferential rather than constraining, so a reasoner will not complain; it will silently infer that every MHPKG consumption value IS a study. SHACL cannot see this at all. Recorded as a term request rather than worked around.""" ;
            sh:in ( oeo:OEO_00000292 oeo:OEO_00000211 oeo:OEO_00000220 oeo:OEO_00010214 oeo:OEO_00020050 ) ;
            sh:maxCount 1 ;
            sh:minCount 1 ;
            sh:order 3 ;
            sh:path oeo:OEO_00000523 ],
        [ sh:datatype xsd:integer ;
            sh:description """The year the value is stated for. WPG Annex 2 III requires the target-scenario indicators for 2030, 2035, 2040 and 2045 unless otherwise specified; an inventory analysis states them for a past base year.
The floor was 2024 while only target scenarios held values. The 2026-09-15 draft puts the same value classes into the aggregated inventory analysis too, whose base years lie in the past, and a generated shape constrains a CLASS, not the container it sits in — so the floor here is now 1990 (the Kyoto base year, the earliest a German inventory reports against), and "a target-scenario value is for 2024 or later" moved to the hand-written `mhpkg_context.shacl.ttl`, which can follow the edge from the scenario to its values.
MISMATCH, and the worst of the three — OEO `has scenario year value` declares domain `scenario factsheet` (oeo:OEO_00000365) AND range `xsd:dateTime`. This slot uses it on a consumption value with an `xsd:integer`, so both ends are wrong. A year is a temporal region, and BFO has `one-dimensional temporal region`; what is missing is a relation from a value to it.""" ;
            sh:maxCount 1 ;
            sh:maxInclusive 2100 ;
            sh:minCount 1 ;
            sh:minInclusive 1990 ;
            sh:nodeKind sh:Literal ;
            sh:order 6 ;
            sh:path oeo:OEO_00020440 ],
        [ sh:description """OEO `has temporal resolution` — Termboard's `has temporal resolution`, `annual` on every value in the 2026-09-15 draft. Optional: a heat plan rarely states it, because WPG Annex 2 asks for annual figures throughout.
MISMATCH — declared domain `data set`. Same class of problem as the `covers …` relations: a reasoner would infer every value is a data set. Folded into TERM REQUEST 4.""" ;
            sh:in ( oeo:OEO_00020161 ) ;
            sh:maxCount 1 ;
            sh:order 8 ;
            sh:path oeo:OEO_00000516 ],
        [ sh:description "OEO `has unit`, domain `quantity value`, range `unit`. Exact fit." ;
            sh:in ( oeo:OEO_00050008 obo:UO_0000224 oeo:OEO_00050011 ) ;
            sh:maxCount 1 ;
            sh:minCount 1 ;
            sh:order 2 ;
            sh:path oeo:OEO_00040010 ],
        [ sh:description "The instance IRI, minted by the three-tier pure function of the IRI policy." ;
            sh:maxCount 1 ;
            sh:nodeKind sh:IRI ;
            sh:order 0 ;
            sh:path mhpkg_schema:id ] ;
    sh:targetClass oeo:OEO_00050016 .

oeo:OEO_00340065 a sh:NodeShape ;
    rdfs:comment """A greenhouse gas emission value — Treibhausgasemissionen, WPG Annex 2 III.2, "in tonnes of CO2 equivalent". OEO: an emission value that quantifies a greenhouse gas emission rate and has a mass unit. Termboard's `greenhouse gas emission value`, in both the inventory analysis and the target scenario.
⚠️ OEO also has `carbon dioxide equivalent quantity value` (OEO_00140083), which is what "tCO2eq" literally is. The class follows the Termboard name; whether every MHPKG emission figure is CO2-equivalent — and therefore should be typed with the narrower class — is a modelling call for the two people drafting the model, not for this schema.
Carrier, sector and technology are OPTIONAL here, unlike on a consumption value: WPG asks for total emissions, with no breakdown. The year and aggregation stay required, because an emission figure without a year is not a figure.""" ;
    sh:closed true ;
    sh:ignoredProperties ( rdf:type ) ;
    sh:property [ sh:description "OEO `covers sector`. Same mismatch as `covers_energy_carrier` — declared domain `study`. WPG Annex 2 III.1 requires the final energy consumption differentiated by final energy sector, so the slot is unavoidable; only the relation is borrowed." ;
            sh:in ( oeo:OEO_00000214 oeo:OEO_00000227 oeo:OEO_00000128 ) ;
            sh:maxCount 1 ;
            sh:order 4 ;
            sh:path oeo:OEO_00000505 ],
        [ sh:description "OEO `has aggregation type`. Declares no domain, so no unintended inference." ;
            sh:in ( oeo:OEO_00140070 oeo:OEO_00140071 oeo:OEO_00140069 oeo:OEO_00140072 oeo:OEO_00140073 ) ;
            sh:maxCount 1 ;
            sh:minCount 1 ;
            sh:order 7 ;
            sh:path oeo:OEO_00390023 ],
        [ sh:datatype xsd:float ;
            sh:description "OEO `has number`, a datatype property whose declared domain is `quantity value`. Exact fit." ;
            sh:maxCount 1 ;
            sh:minCount 1 ;
            sh:nodeKind sh:Literal ;
            sh:order 1 ;
            sh:path oeo:OEO_00140178 ],
        [ sh:description "OEO `has unit`, domain `quantity value`, range `unit`. Exact fit." ;
            sh:in ( oeo:OEO_00010137 ) ;
            sh:maxCount 1 ;
            sh:minCount 1 ;
            sh:order 2 ;
            sh:path oeo:OEO_00040010 ],
        [ sh:datatype xsd:integer ;
            sh:description """The year the value is stated for. WPG Annex 2 III requires the target-scenario indicators for 2030, 2035, 2040 and 2045 unless otherwise specified; an inventory analysis states them for a past base year.
The floor was 2024 while only target scenarios held values. The 2026-09-15 draft puts the same value classes into the aggregated inventory analysis too, whose base years lie in the past, and a generated shape constrains a CLASS, not the container it sits in — so the floor here is now 1990 (the Kyoto base year, the earliest a German inventory reports against), and "a target-scenario value is for 2024 or later" moved to the hand-written `mhpkg_context.shacl.ttl`, which can follow the edge from the scenario to its values.
MISMATCH, and the worst of the three — OEO `has scenario year value` declares domain `scenario factsheet` (oeo:OEO_00000365) AND range `xsd:dateTime`. This slot uses it on a consumption value with an `xsd:integer`, so both ends are wrong. A year is a temporal region, and BFO has `one-dimensional temporal region`; what is missing is a relation from a value to it.""" ;
            sh:maxCount 1 ;
            sh:maxInclusive 2100 ;
            sh:minCount 1 ;
            sh:minInclusive 1990 ;
            sh:nodeKind sh:Literal ;
            sh:order 6 ;
            sh:path oeo:OEO_00020440 ],
        [ sh:description """OEO `covers energy carrier`.
MISMATCH — its declared domain is `study` (oeo:OEO_00020011), and the subject here is a consumption value, not a study. OWL domains are inferential rather than constraining, so a reasoner will not complain; it will silently infer that every MHPKG consumption value IS a study. SHACL cannot see this at all. Recorded as a term request rather than worked around.""" ;
            sh:in ( oeo:OEO_00000292 oeo:OEO_00000211 oeo:OEO_00000220 oeo:OEO_00010214 oeo:OEO_00020050 ) ;
            sh:maxCount 1 ;
            sh:order 3 ;
            sh:path oeo:OEO_00000523 ],
        [ sh:description """OEO `covers technology` — Termboard's `refers to technology`. Optional: WPG Annex 2 III asks for carriers and sectors, not technologies, but heat plans break consumption and emissions down by heat generation technology often enough that the 2026-09-15 draft draws it on every value.
MISMATCH — declared domain `study`, exactly like `covers energy carrier` and `covers sector`. Folded into TERM REQUEST 4.""" ;
            sh:in ( oeo:OEO_00020308 oeo:OEO_00020486 oeo:OEO_00020307 oeo:OEO_00020306 oeo:OEO_00020487 oeo:OEO_00020491 oeo:OEO_00020490 oeo:OEO_00020493 oeo:OEO_00020492 ) ;
            sh:maxCount 1 ;
            sh:order 5 ;
            sh:path oeo:OEO_00390101 ],
        [ sh:description """OEO `has temporal resolution` — Termboard's `has temporal resolution`, `annual` on every value in the 2026-09-15 draft. Optional: a heat plan rarely states it, because WPG Annex 2 asks for annual figures throughout.
MISMATCH — declared domain `data set`. Same class of problem as the `covers …` relations: a reasoner would infer every value is a data set. Folded into TERM REQUEST 4.""" ;
            sh:in ( oeo:OEO_00020161 ) ;
            sh:maxCount 1 ;
            sh:order 8 ;
            sh:path oeo:OEO_00000516 ],
        [ sh:description "The instance IRI, minted by the three-tier pure function of the IRI policy." ;
            sh:maxCount 1 ;
            sh:nodeKind sh:IRI ;
            sh:order 0 ;
            sh:path mhpkg_schema:id ] ;
    sh:targetClass oeo:OEO_00340065 .


